FAILURES
F1 — WCAG 2.5.3 Label in Name (WCAG 2.2 AA baseline in ACCESSIBILITY.md).
File: web/templates/pages/dashboard.html:26.
The newly focusable import drop zone visibly reads:
  Or drop CSV or backup ZIP files anywhere on this page, or click to browse
Its new aria-label instead supplies:
  Choose CSV or backup ZIP files to import
The accessible name does not contain the visible label, including the action
text "click to browse". Speech-input users cannot reliably address the control
using its displayed label. Enter and Space keyboard activation themselves work.

Reproduction: `rtk proxy node focused.cjs` from /tmp/DI3-a11y.mBCqsi.
This loads the actual Dashboard from the isolated synthetic server, injects
axe-core, and explicitly runs rule label-content-name-mismatch. BOTH themes
produce a violation targeting #drop-zone: "Text inside the element is not
included in the accessible name". The probe separately records visible text,
aria-label and keyboard activation. Exact evidence: focused.json.
Standard reference: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/label-in-name.html

Attribution: `rtk proxy git diff master -- web/templates/pages/dashboard.html`
in the source worktree, plus comparison to /tmp/budget2-DI3-base.rhoTJM and
/tmp/DI3-attempt1-review.diff, all identify the role/tabindex/aria-label as DI3
additions. This is introduced by DI3, not an accepted DI1/DI2/DI6 defect.
Relevant unified diff (unchanged visible label follows this hunk):
--- a/web/templates/pages/dashboard.html
+++ b/web/templates/pages/dashboard.html
@@ -26,3 +26,3 @@
-    <div id="drop-zone"
+    <div id="drop-zone" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Choose CSV or backup ZIP files to import"
         class="border border-dashed border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-600 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-center transition-all duration-200 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 hover:border-accent hover:bg-accent-soft cursor-pointer">
-        <input type="file" id="file-input" accept=".csv,.zip" class="hidden">
+        <input type="file" id="file-input" aria-label="CSV or backup ZIP files" accept=".csv,.zip" class="hidden">

